/Alt (Three line graphs labeled A, B, and C show physiological measurement trends across altitudes of 500m, 2560m, 3460m, and 4014m. Graph A depicts SpO2 percentages decreasing with altitude. Graph B illustrates systolic blood pressure trends, while Graph C shows diastolic blood pressure. Blue lines represent migrants, and yellow lines represent residents. Solid and dashed lines indicate standard devices and smartwatches, respectively. Error bars are present.)
